1
00:00:01,814 --> 00:00:03,188
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:03,254 --> 00:00:05,900
Today, a quick tutorial on the "glide".

3
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:13,685
[Music]

4
00:00:13,751 --> 00:00:16,946
To start, you can learn
the classic "glide",

5
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:23,182
with your foot out
in front of the frame,

6
00:00:23,387 --> 00:00:24,750
and the other foot right here.

7
00:00:28,587 --> 00:00:31,652
The best way to learn the "glide"
is to start on "one foot",

8
00:00:32,090 --> 00:00:34,593
pushing on the tire as hard as you can,

9
00:00:34,843 --> 00:00:37,620
then keeping your foot on it
and letting it slide.

10
00:00:38,474 --> 00:00:41,088
At first, you'll only manage
a tiny "glide",

11
00:00:41,154 --> 00:00:43,221
but over time,
it'll get longer and longer.

12
00:00:44,394 --> 00:00:46,794
To "glide", you don't need
much weight on the tire.

13
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:49,320
Just rest your foot on it
and it'll slide on its own.

14
00:00:49,386 --> 00:00:55,801
[Music]

15
00:00:55,867 --> 00:01:02,405
Once you've got the hang
of keeping your foot on the wheel,

16
00:01:02,650 --> 00:01:04,467
you can also try it downhill.

17
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,900
That gives you more speed
and longer "glides".

18
00:01:09,774 --> 00:01:12,301
If there's no slope nearby,

19
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:18,575
you can just ride fast
and then place your feet to "glide",

20
00:01:19,021 --> 00:01:23,600
like this.

21
00:01:25,513 --> 00:01:26,803
Teleportation!

22
00:01:27,081 --> 00:01:30,440
You can also learn to "glide"
by getting someone to tow you.

23
00:01:30,506 --> 00:01:40,275
[Music]

24
00:01:40,341 --> 00:01:44,257
Once you're doing well
with someone towing you,

25
00:01:44,281 --> 00:01:47,087
you can let go of them
once you're in position.

26
00:01:47,153 --> 00:01:56,135
[Music]

27
00:01:56,201 --> 00:01:59,763
Next, once you've mastered
the classic "glide",

28
00:02:00,061 --> 00:02:02,855
you can bring your foot back
onto the frame.

29
00:02:02,994 --> 00:02:08,095
That will set you up
for the "stand up glide" later on.

30
00:02:08,381 --> 00:02:13,760
So you'll go from this,
the classic "glide", to this.

31
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:21,275
To "glide" longer
with your foot on the frame,

32
00:02:21,367 --> 00:02:25,826
build up speed by riding fast,
then put both feet on the frame.

33
00:02:27,921 --> 00:02:30,447
To get back on the pedals,
whether from the classic "glide"

34
00:02:30,513 --> 00:02:32,034
or the "foot-on-frame glide",

35
00:02:32,058 --> 00:02:34,787
it works exactly
like a regular "wheel walk".

36
00:02:34,853 --> 00:02:41,721
[Music]

37
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:45,348
Once you can "glide",
you can learn to "coast".

38
00:02:46,547 --> 00:02:49,821
It's exactly the same thing...
well, almost,

39
00:02:49,940 --> 00:02:52,920
except your foot
doesn't touch the tire.

40
00:02:52,986 --> 00:03:42,262
[Music]

